1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,800
Is Subsequence — LeetCode 392

2
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:06,200
Problem: is s a subsequence of t? Keep t's order, delete some letters, and land on s.

3
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:10,200
Example: s = "abc", t = "ahbgdc". The a, b and c all appear in order.

4
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:13,600
Key idea: one pointer on each string.

5
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:18,000
Scan t with j. When t[j] is the character s needs, tick it off and advance i.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,500
If i ticks off all of s, then s is a subsequence.

7
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:24,500
i needs 'a': t starts with 'a' — match. Advance i to 'b'.

8
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:28,000
t's 'h' isn't 'b', skip it. Then 'b' matches — advance i to 'c'.

9
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,500
Skip 'g', skip 'd', then 'c' matches — i has cleared all of s.

10
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:36,000
Every character of s was found in order, so the answer is true.

11
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,500
Bonus, cleaner code: one counter and a single sweep of t with a range-for.

12
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:44,500
Time O(n) over t, O(1) space.

13
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:49,000
